# Wuzzkang AI Coding Rules & Master Orchestrator

You are an AI Assistant working on the Wuzzkang monorepo.
To ensure quality, architectural consistency, and strict compliance, you MUST follow the rules in this workspace:

## 1. Onboarding & Core Philosophy
- Before making any code changes, read `wuzzkang-engineering/AI_BOOTSTRAP.md` and `wuzzkang-engineering/docs/00_FOUNDATION.md`.

## 2. Master Skill Orchestrator (Automatic Skill Execution)
Before executing code, inspect the corresponding skill under `wuzzkang-engineering/skills/`:
- **Token Optimization & Efficiency Guard**: `wuzzkang-token-optimization-guard/SKILL.md`
- **Code Refactoring & Modernization**: `wuzzkang-code-refactor/SKILL.md`
- **Senior Tech Lead Code Reviewer**: `wuzzkang-code-reviewer/SKILL.md`
- **Refactoring & Multi-Version Architecture**: `wuzzkang-multi-version-architecture/SKILL.md`
- **Active Workspace & Progress Tracking**: `wuzzkang-implementation-protocol/SKILL.md`
- **New Products / Templates**: `wuzzkang-product-template-generator/SKILL.md`
- **V2 Modular Section Builder**: `wuzzkang-v2-section-builder/SKILL.md`
- **AI Platform Compilers & BullMQ Worker**: `wuzzkang-ai-platform-compiler/SKILL.md`
- **UI Component Guard & Credit Safety**: `wuzzkang-ui-standards-guard/SKILL.md`
- **DoD Audit & Doc Sync**: `wuzzkang-doc-sync-auditor/SKILL.md`

## 3. STRICT USER SAFETY & OPERATIONAL RULES
1. **Mandatory Testing (Performance, Security, & Scalability):** Every code change or feature addition MUST be tested after completion before declaring done. All testing MUST evaluate three core dimensions: Performance, Security, and Scalability.
2. **Node.js Environment (>= 24):** Always use Node.js version >= 24 (`nvm use 24`).
3. **Test Server Cleanup:** After finishing debug/test execution of any local dev server (`npm run dev`, `node server.js`), AI MUST kill/terminate the background process to prevent port conflicts with local servers.
4. **Database Protection:** NEVER drop tables, truncate databases, or alter sensitive schemas without explicit user approval.
5. **User Confirmation:** Any technical action or suggestion outside explicit user commands MUST be confirmed first.
6. **Credential Protection:** Inspect all code to guarantee NO API keys, Private keys, or secrets are exposed or committed to Git.
7. **Mandatory Local Git Commit (Strictly NO Push):** Every time a task or milestone is completed, AI MUST execute a local `git commit` with a clean Conventional Commit message. AI is STRICTLY FORBIDDEN from executing `git push`.

## 4. Critical UI & Database Rules
- **UI Component Reuse:** Re-use `<ImagePickerField>` linked to `handleUploadImage` (signed URL flow).
- **FAQ AI Generation:** Implement safe-merging so user-filled Q&A are never overwritten by AI.
- **Credit Cost:** Database `cost` fields must be in Credit units, not raw IDR Rupiah nominals.

## 5. Definition of Done (Document Updates)
Before ending your turn, verify and update the corresponding documentation files in `wuzzkang-engineering/docs/` (`05_API_SPECIFICATION.md`, `09_DATABASE_ARCHITECTURE.md`, `07_RENDER_ENGINE.md`, `02_CURRENT_STATE.md`, `08_REPOSITORY_MAP.md`).

## 6. Implementation Workspace Lifecycle
Always follow the active/archive workflow in `./implementation/` (`implementation/active/` for ongoing work, `implementation/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-feature-name/` on completion).

## 7. Communication
- Respond to the user in **Bahasa Indonesia**.
- Keep engineering artifacts in **English**.
